code.description:
The Playwright code to execute. Must be an async function declaration that takes a page parameter.

Example:
async function run(page) {
  console.log(await page.title());
  return await page.title();
}

Returns an object with:
- result: The return value from your function
- logs: Array of console logs from execution
- errors: Array of any errors encountered

Example response:
{"result": "Google", "logs": ["[log] Google"], "errors": []}
